    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0435" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/946</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-15">July 15, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Cordell</hi>: I am enclosing herewith, for
                    your information, a copy of a memorandum I have presented to the President
                    dealing <pb facs="0436" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/> with the Chinese request to
                    purchase $200 million of gold out of the $500 million financial aid as a means
                    of helping to check inflation in China.</p>
                <p>I am also enclosing a copy of cable, dated July 14, 1943, dealing with this
                    matter sent to the Treasury representative in China through your
                        Department.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d351-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Morgenthau, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d351-a1.xml" xpointer="d351-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d351-f1" n="34" xml:id="d351-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 911, July 16, 9 p.m., to the Chargé in China, <ref
                        target="#pg428">p. 428</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
